# Architecture: DynamicModelTable — Metadata Strategy & Table Building

> [!NOTE]
> This document is a deep-dive into how `DynamicModelTable` uses backend metadata to automatically build a fully-featured data table — from GraphQL introspection to final pixel rendering.

---

## 1. High-Level Data Flow

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["app + model props"] --> B["MetadataProvider"]
    B --> C["useTableMetadata()"]
    C --> D["Phase 1: Bootstrap Query<br/>(fields, relationships, basic filterConfig)"]
    C --> E["Phase 2: Capabilities Query<br/>(filters, mutations, permissions, templates)"]
    C --> F["Persisted Cache<br/>(localStorage fallback)"]
    
    D --> G["Merged & Normalized<br/>ModelSchema"]
    E --> G
    F --> G
    
    G --> H["TableProvider<br/>(state: filters, pagination, visibility)"]
    H --> I["useTableColumns()<br/>(metadata → columnDefs)"]
    H --> J["useTableQueryConfig()<br/>(visibility → field masking)"]
    I --> J
    J --> K["useTableData()<br/>(GraphQL data query execution)"]
    
    I --> L["dynamicColumns memo<br/>(columnDefs → DynamicTableColumnInput)"]
    K --> L
    L --> M["DynamicTable render"]

    style D fill:#4ade80,color:#000
    style E fill:#60a5fa,color:#000
    style F fill:#fbbf24,color:#000
    style G fill:#a78bfa,color:#000
```

---

## 2. Two-Phase Metadata Loading Strategy

The metadata loading in [useTableMetadata.ts](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/hooks/useTableMetadata.ts) is split into **two distinct GraphQL queries** for performance optimization:

### Phase 1 — Bootstrap (Immediate)

Defined in [queries.ts](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/shared/api/graphql/graphql/metadata/queries.ts#L98-L181) as `TABLE_BOOTSTRAP_METADATA_QUERY`.

```mermaid
graph LR
    A["Component Mount"] -->|"useQuery (cache-first)"| B["Bootstrap Query"]
    B --> C["Fields: name, fieldName, verboseName,<br/>fieldType, graphqlType, choices,<br/>visibility, isRelation, etc."]
    B --> D["Relationships: name, relatedApp,<br/>relatedModel, lookupField, etc."]
    B --> E["FilterConfig: inputTypeName,<br/>supportsQuick only"]
    B --> F["Basic: app, model, verboseName,<br/>primaryKey, ordering"]
```

**Fetched immediately** on mount. Contains just enough to:
- Build column headers (field names, verbose names, types)
- Determine field type for cell rendering (isDate, isNumeric, choices, etc.)
- Know about relationships for nested accessors
- Enable quick search if supported

### Phase 2 — Capabilities (Lazy / Idle)

Defined in [queries.ts](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/shared/api/graphql/graphql/metadata/queries.ts#L183-L320) as `TABLE_CAPABILITIES_METADATA_QUERY`.

```mermaid
graph LR
    A["Browser Idle<br/>requestIdleCallback"] -->|"useLazyQuery"| B["Capabilities Query"]
    B --> C["Full FilterConfig:<br/>style, supports*, presets,<br/>computedFilters"]
    B --> D["Filters:<br/>per-field filter options,<br/>operators, types"]
    B --> E["Mutations:<br/>CRUD operations,<br/>input fields, permissions"]
    B --> F["Permissions:<br/>canList, canCreate,<br/>canUpdate, canDelete, etc."]
    B --> G["Templates:<br/>export templates, guards"]
    B --> H["FieldGroups:<br/>field grouping config"]
```

**Deferred** until the browser is idle via `requestIdleCallback` (fallback: `setTimeout(80ms)`). This is the "heavy" payload needed for:
- Advanced filtering UI
- CRUD mutation dialogs
- Permission-gated actions
- Template/export features

### Merge Strategy

```typescript
// From useTableMetadata.ts lines 150-181
const base = bootstrapMetadata ?? persistedMetadata;  // 1. Bootstrap or cached
const merged = {
  ...base,                          // 2. Spread base fields
  ...(capabilitiesMetadata ?? {}),  // 3. Overlay capabilities
  filterConfig: {                   // 4. Deep-merge filterConfig
    ...(base.filterConfig ?? {}),
    ...(capabilitiesMetadata?.filterConfig ?? {}),
  },
};
const normalized = normalizeModelSchema(merged, { app, model });
```

> [!TIP]
> **Referential Stability**: A JSON signature (`stableMetadataCacheRef`) prevents unnecessary re-renders when the merged result hasn't actually changed.

### Persisted Cache (Instant Fallback)

Before any network request resolves, [persisted-cache.ts](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/shared/api/graphql/graphql/metadata/persisted-cache.ts) provides a **localStorage snapshot** from the last session:

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["Component Mount"] --> B{"Bootstrap query<br/>already cached?"}
    B -->|Yes| C["Use Apollo cache"]
    B -->|No| D{"localStorage has<br/>persisted metadata?"}
    D -->|Yes| E["Use persisted cache<br/>(instant render)"]
    D -->|No| F["Show LoadingSkeleton"]
    C --> G["Render table immediately"]
    E --> G
```

This creates a **three-tier fallback**: Apollo cache → localStorage → loading skeleton.

---

## 3. MetadataProvider — Post-Processing

The [MetadataProvider](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/context/MetadataContext.tsx#L31-L70) sits between raw metadata and consumers:

```typescript
const mergedMetadata = useMemo(
  () => normalizeModelSchemaAccessors(
    mergeModelSchemaWithRelationships(metadata),
  ),
  [metadata],
);
```

| Step | Function | Purpose |
|------|----------|---------|
| 1 | `mergeModelSchemaWithRelationships()` | Injects relationship info into field entries for unified access |
| 2 | `normalizeModelSchemaAccessors()` | Converts field names to canonical camelCase GraphQL format |

The context exposes:

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| [metadata](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/components/DynamicModelTable.tsx#1334-1337) | `ModelSchema?` | Fully normalized schema |
| [loading](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/components/DynamicModelTable.tsx#1322-1325) | `boolean` | Bootstrap still loading |
| `error` | `Error?` | Bootstrap failure |
| `capabilitiesLoading` | `boolean` | Phase 2 in progress |
| `capabilitiesLoaded` | `boolean` | Phase 2 complete |
| `scheduleCapabilitiesPrefetch` | [() => void](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/components/DynamicModelTable.tsx#1313-1316) | Trigger idle prefetch |
| `ensureCapabilitiesLoaded` | [() => Promise](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/components/DynamicModelTable.tsx#1313-1316) | Force load capabilities |

