## 5. Column Building Pipeline

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph "Step 1: useTableColumns"
        M["ModelSchema<br/>(metadata)"] --> CD["BaseModelTableColumnDef[]<br/>(accessor, title, render)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Step 2: useTableQueryConfig"
        CD --> VA["visibleAccessors[]<br/>(field masking for query)"]
        VA --> RA["requiredAccessors[]<br/>(always-fetch: PK, grouping)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Step 3: useTableData"
        VA --> QV["Query Variables<br/>(page, perPage, where,<br/>orderBy, fields)"]
        RA --> QV
        QV --> GQL["GraphQL Data Query"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Step 4: dynamicColumns"
        CD --> DC["DynamicTableColumnInput[]"]
        GQL --> DC
    end
```

### Step 1: [useTableColumns()](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/hooks/useTableColumns.ts#29-276) – Metadata → Column Definitions

[useTableColumns.ts](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/hooks/useTableColumns.ts) transforms [ModelSchema](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/types.ts#258-293) into renderable column definitions:

| Input | Output |
|-------|--------|
| `metadata.fields[]` | `BaseModelTableColumnDef[]` with [accessor](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/components/DynamicModelTable.tsx#806-807), [id](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/types.ts#15-20), `title` |
| `fields` config (include/exclude/add) | Filtered & ordered column list |
| `relations` config | Nested accessor paths (e.g., `client.name`) |

Key operations:
- **Field canonicalization**: Converts snake_case → camelCase via `toGraphqlFieldName()`
- **Relation count resolution**: Maps synthetic `orderItemsCount` to underlying `orderItems` relation
- **Custom render support**: User-provided render functions override defaults
- **Exclude filtering**: Removes explicitly excluded fields

### Step 2: [useTableQueryConfig()](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/hooks/useTableQueryConfig.ts#30-207) – Visibility → Field Masking

[useTableQueryConfig.ts](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/hooks/useTableQueryConfig.ts) determines **which fields to request** in the GraphQL query:

```
All metadata fields
  → Filter by visibility (user prefs / persisted state / defaults)
  → Add required accessors (primaryKey, grouping field)
  → Add synthetic relation count sources
  → Final: visibleAccessors[] + requiredAccessors[]
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is a critical optimization — only visible columns are fetched from the backend, reducing payload and DB load.

### Step 3: [useTableData()](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/hooks/useTableData.ts#81-226) – Query Execution

[useTableData.ts](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/hooks/useTableData.ts) executes the actual data query:

```typescript
useModelPageQuery({
  identity: { app, model, managerName },
  metadataOptions: { metadata, metadataProfile: "table" },
  selectionOptions: { fields: selectionFields, relations },
  variables: { page, perPage, quick, where, presets, orderBy, ... },
});
```

- Supports **pagination** and **infinite scroll** modes
- Debounces quick search (300ms)
- Handles data deduplication for infinite scroll merging

### Step 4: `dynamicColumns` Memo – Final Column Assembly

At [line 782](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/components/DynamicModelTable.tsx#L782-L882), column definitions are transformed into `DynamicTableColumnInput[]`:

```typescript
columnDefs.map((column) => ({
  id: column.id,
  headerMode: "custom",
  title: column.title,
  accessorFn: (row) => resolveValueOptimized(row, accessorPath),
  header: () => <TableColumnMenu ... /> + <ColumnFilter ... />,
  cell: ({ row, value }) => {
    // 1. Try custom render function
    // 2. Try field-type-aware formatCellValue()
    // 3. Fallback: formatFallbackCellValue()
    // 4. Wrap in RelationStatsHover if applicable
  },
}));
```

---

## 6. Lookup Maps for O(1) Metadata Access

Two lookup maps are built at render time for efficient per-cell metadata access:

### `fieldLookup` (Map\<string, FieldSchema\>)

```typescript
// Line 652-672: Maps ALL name variants → FieldSchema
// Keys: field.name, field.fieldName, normalized(name), normalized(fieldName)
```

Used in the cell renderer to find the correct [FieldSchema](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/types.ts#31-101) for type-aware formatting (dates, booleans, choices, numerics, etc.).

### `relationLookup` (Map\<string, RelationDescriptor\>)

```typescript
// Line 674-712: Maps ALL name variants → { relatedApp, relatedModel, isToMany, ... }
```

Used for:
- `RelationStatsHover` — showing count stats on relation cells
- Determining if a column represents a to-many relation

---

## 7. Cell Rendering Strategy

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Cell Value"] --> B{"Has custom<br/>render fn?"}
    B -->|Yes| C["column.render(value, row, ctx)"]
    B -->|No| D{"Field metadata<br/>found?"}
    D -->|Yes| E["formatCellValue(value, field)"]
    D -->|No| F["formatFallbackCellValue(value)"]
    
    C --> G{"Is relation<br/>stats column?"}
    E --> G
    F --> G
    
    G -->|Yes| H["Wrap in RelationStatsHover"]
    G -->|No| I["Render directly"]
```

### `formatCellValue(value, field)` handles:

| Field Type | Rendering |
|------------|-----------|
| `isDate / isDatetime` | Localized date formatting |
| `isBoolean` | ✓ / ✗ indicators |
| `choices` | Resolves value → label |
| `isNumeric` | Number formatting |
| `isFile / isImage` | Link / thumbnail |
| `isJson` | JSON stringify |
| Default | String conversion |

---

## 8. State Management Flow

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph "DynamicTable (TanStack)"
        TS["Table State Changes"]
    end
    
    subgraph "handleStateChange"
        TS --> CO["columnOrder"]
        TS --> CV["columnVisibility"]
        TS --> CW["columnSizing"]
        TS --> RS["rowSelection"]
        TS --> PG["pagination"]
        TS --> DM["dragMode"]
        TS --> DN["density"]
        TS --> WC["wrapCells"]
        TS --> EX["expanded"]
    end
    
    subgraph "TableProvider (Context)"
        CO --> TP["Centralized State"]
        CV --> TP
        CW --> TP
        RS --> TP
        PG --> TP
        DM --> TP
        DN --> TP
        WC --> TP
        EX --> TP
    end
    
    subgraph "Side Effects"
        TP --> PE["useTablePersistence<br/>(save to user settings)"]
        TP --> QR["useTableData<br/>(re-query on pagination/filter change)"]
    end
```

> [!TIP]
> All state changes go through **equality guards** ([areBooleanMapsEqual](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/components/DynamicModelTable.tsx#332-351), [areNumberMapsEqual](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/components/DynamicModelTable.tsx#352-371), [areStringArraysEqual](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/components/DynamicModelTable.tsx#317-331), etc.) to prevent unnecessary state updates and re-renders.

