## 9. Section Slot System

The visual layout is composed of **configurable slots** with visibility toggles:

```typescript
const DEFAULT_SECTION_VISIBILITY = {
  header: true,        // ModelTableHeader (title, description, icon)
  topActions: true,    // Create button, custom actions
  toolbar: true,       // Quick search, filters, display options
  bulkActionsBar: true,// Bulk delete, export, etc.
  footer: false,       // Optional footer
  dialogs: true,       // Create/Update/Delete dialogs
};
```

Each slot can be replaced via `content.slots`:

```typescript
const HeaderSlot = content?.slots?.Header ?? ModelTableHeader;
const TopActionsSlot = content?.slots?.TopActions ?? ModelTableTopActions;
const ToolbarSlot = content?.slots?.Toolbar ?? ModelTableToolbarSection;
// ... etc.
```

---

## 10. Summary: Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|----------|-----------|
| **Two-phase metadata loading** | Fast initial render (columns visible) while heavy capabilities load in background |
| **LocalStorage fallback** | Instant table skeleton even before first network response |
| **Field masking** | Only query visible columns — reduces backend load |
| **Canonical accessor normalization** | Handles snake_case ↔ camelCase mismatches seamlessly |
| **Lookup maps** | O(1) field/relation resolution during cell rendering |
| **Equality guards** | Prevents cascade re-renders from TanStack state changes |
| **Imperative handle** | Parent components can [refetch()](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/components/DynamicModelTable.tsx#1328-1334) or read [data](file:///e:/Projects/libraries/rail-react/src/widgets/model-table/components/DynamicModelTable.tsx#1313-1316) without prop drilling |
| **Slot system** | Every visual section is replaceable for customization |
| **requestIdleCallback** | Capabilities prefetch doesn't block user interaction |
